Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a line of the analytic intersection between two blends that goes
round a periodic surface's period outside its domain is not taken as the
curve between the ends; the next line, or the walk from the ends, is
(mitcad#2009).

A pad's end face whose top edge (between two planes) and side edge (an
arc, the pad's outer wall a cylinder) are rounded with 0.5, the corner
where the two roundings meet built by PerformTwoCornerbyInter: the curve
between the rounding of the straight edge (a cylinder whose domain is a
quarter turn, its contacts at u = 0 and u = pi/2) and the rounding of the
arc (a torus) is ChFi3d_ComputeCurves' analytic intersection (GeomInt_IntSS
of the two bounded surfaces). Its ends lie on the cylinder's domain
boundary, at u = 0 and u = pi/2. Depending on the last bits of the input
(the same pad on a body built with a bend radius of 31, 32, 34, 37, 41, 42,
43 or 44 instead of 30, 33, 35, 36, 38 to 40 or 45), GeomInt's line ran
from u = 4 pi down to 5 pi / 2: between the right ends, but the other way
round the cylinder, three quarters of a turn outside the domain. The
rounding's face was trimmed by that curve: the shape checked valid, but
the rounding of the straight edge covered three quarters of its cylinder,
reached 3.8 beyond the pad's end and added 4.8 mm3 to the body instead of
taking 0.33 away.

- ChFi3d_LeavesPeriodicDomain: whether a line's pcurve, at nine points
  inside its trimmed range, leaves the surface's domain in a periodic
  direction by more than a hundredth of the period, each point brought
  into the period that starts at the domain's start (a domain of a whole
  period is never left).
- ChFi3d_ComputeCurves: in GeomInt's lines, after the ends are found on a
  line and before it is trimmed, a line that leaves either surface's
  domain so is passed over: the next line is tried, then, as when no line
  fits, the walk between the known ends (IntWalk_PWalking), which stays
  inside the domains. A line inside them is taken as before.
- No catch is added.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1800.

